# Production Safety Rules

## Protected resources
- main branch, Vercel Production and the production Supabase project are protected.
- Never deploy, merge, push, or alter production unless explicitly instructed.
- Never run destructive or state-changing database commands against production.

## Database changes
- Every schema, function, trigger, view, grant and RLS change must be a migration.
- Do not make untracked changes in the remote Supabase Dashboard.
- Use expand -> migrate/backfill -> contract for breaking schema changes.
- Add new fields before changing application reads/writes.
- Drop or rename old fields only in a later release.
- Regenerate database TypeScript types after every schema change.
- Include foreign keys, indexes, nullability, defaults and deletion behavior explicitly.
- Add database/RLS tests for every policy change.

## Authentication and authorization
- Use browser clients only in client-side code.
- Use request-scoped server clients in Server Components, Server Actions and Route Handlers.
- Never expose secret/service-role keys to the browser.
- Never disable RLS to make application code work.
- Every business query must enforce organization scope.
- Test ADMIN, INSPECTOR, MANAGER and unauthorized roles separately.

## Data correctness
- Do not fetch all rows and filter them in JavaScript when the database can filter.
- Do not use select('*') without a documented reason.
- Do not swallow Supabase errors.
- A mutation is successful only when the expected row was returned or affected.
- Every mutation must define cache invalidation and UI refresh behavior.
- User-specific or organization-specific data must not use a shared cache key.

## Testing
Before marking work complete, run:
- typecheck
- lint
- unit tests
- database/RLS tests
- production build
- relevant Playwright E2E tests

Test critical flows against a production build, not only next dev.

## Change scope
- One root cause per logical commit.
- Do not mix schema migration, broad refactor and UI redesign in one change.
- Every fix must include reproduction, evidence, regression test and rollback note.
- Do not remove existing functionality unless explicitly required.

## Release
- Feature branch -> Pull Request -> staging/preview -> tests -> approval -> production.
- Preview must not write to the production database.
- Production promotion requires passing smoke tests.
- Breaking database changes require backward compatibility with both old and new app versions.
